@startuml Kiwi_Physical_Setup
!theme plain
skinparam backgroundColor white
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam defaultFontName "Latin Modern Roman"
skinparam defaultFontSize 13
skinparam ArrowColor #216875
skinparam packageStyle rectangle
skinparam nodesep 20
skinparam ranksep 24
title Proposed physical test setup and observation boundaries
top to bottom direction
rectangle "Frozen source WAV\n+ expected-frame manifest" as WAV
rectangle "Qualified playback\n+ audio interface" as Playback
rectangle "Transceiver\nverified configuration" as Radio
rectangle "Antenna system" as Ant
rectangle "Remote Kiwi\nantenna + receiver" as Kiwi
rectangle "Local transmit monitor\nrecording + timestamps" as Monitor
rectangle "Station execution\nPTT owner + stop path" as Control
WAV -right-> Playback : audio
Playback -right-> Radio : TX audio
Radio -right-> Ant : RF
Ant -down-> Kiwi : HF path
Radio --> Monitor : qualified monitor path
Control --> Radio : PTT / release
Control --> Monitor : start / stop / fault evidence
note bottom of Monitor
Monitor implementation and calibration
must be qualified.
A generated WAV alone does not prove
RF transmission.
A Kiwi capture is not proof of remote
station receipt.
end note
@enduml
